docs/COMPLETE_STATE_CACHE_DESIGN_2026-07-22.md: field-by-field mutability audit of
BaseDualState/verify (both already fully-owned, non-aliased data by construction -- proven from
solve_base_state/archC_verified_state's own collect/copy calls, already exploited by
cm_checkpoint.jl's last_F_state[] pattern), fingerprint design (draws, W/D/sigma, CM
config/L/grid/basis/contrasts, opt-file CONTENT hash, KNITRO release, schema version; delta and
cm_gradient_backend deliberately excluded, with the reasoning for each), and why no external
OrderedDict/DataStructures.jl dependency is needed for the LRU (small max_entries, O(n) scan is
fine).

complete_state_cache.jl (new, purely additive, opt-in, default off): CompleteStateEntry,
CompleteStateCache, complete_state_fingerprint, complete_state_lookup!/store!, and
archC_verified_state_cached! (a wrapper around the UNMODIFIED archC_verified_state -- identical
behavior to calling it directly when cache=nothing, the default everywhere).

overnight_complete_state_cache_d4_gate.jl: A/B/A restore-vs-fresh-cold-solve, no-aliasing after
subsequent solves mutate live scratch, 7 independent context-mismatch fingerprint checks
(L/probs/contrasts/backend/KNITRO-release/opt-file-content/draws), cross-delta key-independence,
never-store-on-an-inner-solve-failure, bounded LRU eviction correctness, instrumentation
counters. 32/32 pass.

Real finding (not a bug): two INDEPENDENT archC_verified_state solves at the identical x_free0
are NOT bit-for-bit identical to each other (~1e-11 to 1e-13 diffs, KNITRO's own tolerance-based
convergence noise floor) -- the cache's correctness claim is exact restoration of what was
STORED (proven bit-for-bit in the no-aliasing test), not agreement between two independent
solves, which no tolerance-based solver guarantees. Test tolerances set accordingly and
documented inline.

NOT done in this session (see design doc §8 and the final report): wiring into
cm_checkpoint.jl's cb_F!/cb_G!, D=20 hit-rate/wall-value measurement, checkpoint/resume
interaction test, combined CM-C+ + cache gates. Left as a documented, independently-tested
prototype per the task brief's own explicit allowance.
